      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(¬P∧Q)∨R?$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:\n\n$$\n(¬P∧Q)∨R≡(¬P∨R)∧(Q∨R)\n$$\n\nNow, since $¬P∨R≡R∨¬P$ and $Q∨R≡R∨Q$ we can write\n\n$$\n(¬P∨R)∧(Q∨R)≡(R∨¬P)∧(R∨Q).\n$$",
